      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-155999" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4496;         --source-height: 3000;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4496x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff2%2Fe6%2F842c0c584574bebf383c85a84897%2Fap26330589214672.jpg" class="img" alt="Pedestrians shield themselves with umbrellas as they walk in the rain on Thanksgiving Day in New York, Thursday, Nov. 26, 2026." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Pedestrians shield themselves with umbrellas as they walk in the rain on Thanksgiving Day in New York, Thursday, Nov. 26, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Yuki Iwamura/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hundreds of thousands of people are without power&lt;/strong&gt; after a powerful storm &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/27/nx-s1-6054884/thanksgiving-weather-black-friday" target="_blank"&gt;swept through much of the East Coast&lt;/a&gt; and Midwest on Thanksgiving. Hundreds of flights were canceled and thousands were delayed during one of the busiest travel times of the year.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;Flooding caused most of the damage and disruptions, &lt;/strong&gt;NPR's Kat Lonsdorf tells &lt;em&gt;Up First&lt;/em&gt;. Several bridges in New Jersey were shut down, and people were seen kayaking through usually busy streets in parts of coastal Virginia. Exceptionally high tides, known as the King Tides, have been battering the West Coast. Lonsdorf says there's still a lot of work to do before roads return to normal, &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/share/audio/media/nx-s1-6055516:x" target="_blank"&gt;but there is some hope&lt;/a&gt;. The storms should move out and the tides should recede heading into Saturday, as people begin their journeys home.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Despite inflation and concerns about the cost of living, Americans are expected to spend a record amount&lt;/strong&gt; again this year for Black Friday. The National Retail Federation predicts a 4.2% increase in holiday retail sales this year compared with last year.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;NPR's Alina Selyukh says surveys indicate people are cutting back on other spending&lt;/strong&gt; to spend during the holiday season. She notes that while gas and housing costs have been big drivers of inflation, the prices of goods, including gifts, have not risen as dramatically. She also says she's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/share/audio/media/nx-s1-6055516:x" target="_blank"&gt;watching a shift in the trend&lt;/a&gt; of how people are shopping. Although most people are doing their holiday shopping online, more are choosing to shop in person.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Trump administration has banned asylum claims at the U.S.-Mexico border and canceled thousands of pending asylum applications&lt;/strong&gt; over the past nearly two years. Critics say the sweeping immigration changes have all but shut down access to asylum. Soon, the Supreme Court will &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/24/nx-s1-6037854/trump-effectively-ended-asylum-advocates-look-to-the-supreme-court-to-restore-it" target="_blank"&gt;consider whether the president can circumvent Congress&lt;/a&gt; and existing federal immigration law and unilaterally suspend access to asylum protections. In December, Justices will also review the administration's strategy of deporting immigrants to third countries that have agreed to process asylum claims, even as some face human rights abuse allegations and cannot guarantee that the asylum-seeker won't be returned to their home nation.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Behind the story&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-155424" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3733;         --source-height: 2100;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3733x2100+0+390/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F9c%2F3a%2F99324afc42febd0bdf8ef965b3a1%2Fgettyimages-2297767958.jpg" class="img" alt="A pop-up shop for &amp;quot;dots&amp;quot; a personal assistant agent at the OpenAI developers conference on September 29, 2026 in San Francisco, California. Sam Altman announced a new artificial intelligence personal assistant agents named &amp;quot;dots&amp;quot; to rival Meta&amp;#039;s Muse." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A pop-up shop for "dots" a personal assistant agent at the OpenAI developers conference on September 29, 2026 in San Francisco, California. Sam Altman announced a new artificial intelligence personal assistant agents named "dots" to rival Meta's Muse.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Heather Diehl/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This essay was written by  &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/1242808013/stephan-bisaha" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Stephan Bisaha&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;, NPR's personal finance correspondent&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;I was at a book club recently, chatting with a small group, when someone from another circle asked what we were discussing. Driven by an instinct to instigate (perhaps a side effect of our earlier heated book talk), I said the "benefits of AI."&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;After some anti-AI sighs, I told them about a source whose AI agent saved him $50 without him even asking. A friend uses Claude for her retirement funding decisions. Others are turning to AI for holiday shopping.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;New AI agents can now help buy gifts, from brainstorming to checkout. Would I trust AI with my own shopping? Apparently not.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Those cheap acoustic panels AI recommended? Only a good deal if I ignored how tiny they were. The griddle it suggested? Too big. Then I started worrying about how much of my personal data my AI assistant was collecting and eventually asked it to forget everything about me.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Forrester principal analyst Emily Pfeiffer &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/25/nx-s1-6048524/what-to-know-before-using-ai-agents-for-black-friday-shopping" target="_blank"&gt;guided me through another attempt&lt;/a&gt; for my book club's gift exchange.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;I gave Meta's new AI agent, Muse, my requirements: a $25 cap for a Gen Z crowd and something that makes noise, per the organizer's request (way to stereotype the radio reporter).&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Muse's suggestions? A karaoke mic and a plastic, yodeling pickle. I wasn't sold on either.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Once again, my shopping cart is empty.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;My next attempt with AI, though, might not be this holiday season. Instead I'm planning to buy a Tamagotchi for the gift exchange. Remember those virtual keychain pets from the '90s? A throwback to a time when you could take your digital companion shopping without worrying about your privacy.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Weekend picks&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-img-6350581" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3000;         --source-height: 1688;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3000x1688+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F34%2F0a%2Ff2dcdf0e47f39edb8dd104c77b