      <title>Storms disrupt Thanksgiving travel. And, FCC violated ABC's free speech, judge says</title>
      <author>Brittney Melton</author>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/11/26/g-s1-155950/up-first-newsletter-thanksgiving-weather-travel-trump-tariffs-iowa-detonation-fcc-free-speech</link>
      <comments>https://text.npr.org/2026/11/26/g-s1-155950/up-first-newsletter-thanksgiving-weather-travel-trump-tariffs-iowa-detonation-fcc-free-speech</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.npr.org/2026/11/26/g-s1-155950/up-first-newsletter-thanksgiving-weather-travel-trump-tariffs-iowa-detonation-fcc-free-speech</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:24:29 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Severe storms sweeping across the nation threaten to &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/26/nx-s1-6054079/storms-expected-on-both-coasts-as-millions-travel-for-thanksgiving" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;cause widespread travel delays&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; today&lt;/strong&gt;, as millions of people gather with their loved ones. New York City officials announced that the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade &lt;a href="https://gothamist.com/news/530-press?utm_source=npr.org&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=national_highlight&amp;utm_content=homepage" target="_blank"&gt;has been rescheduled&lt;/a&gt; to Saturday due to the threat of powerful wind gusts that could reach up to 60 mph. This year marked the 100th procession, and the first time the iconic event is being postponed.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-155947" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 8466;         --source-height: 4762;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8466x4762+0+441/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Fa4%2F4e%2Fd1653db84a76bcc9f17e6dbf78cb%2Fgettyimages-2306291610.jpg" class="img" alt="Workers inflate the Spider-Man balloon during Macy&amp;#039;s Balloon Inflation 2026 on November 25, 2026 in New York City. Macy&amp;#039;s plans to celebrate its 100th Thanksgiving Day Parade with a record 100 inflatables, but forecasted high winds are threatening to ground the giant balloons." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Workers inflate the Spider-Man balloon during Macy's Balloon Inflation 2026 on November 25, 2026 in New York City. Macy's plans to celebrate its 100th Thanksgiving Day Parade with a record 100 inflatables, but forecasted high winds are threatening to ground the giant balloons.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Adam Gray/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;Something is happening across almost every part of the country right now&lt;/strong&gt;, NPR's Kat Lonsdorf tells &lt;em&gt;Up First&lt;/em&gt;. Extreme high tides are affecting the West Coast, snow is expected in parts of the Midwest, and in the South and Southeast, a major storm is advancing up the East Coast. Meteorologist Richard Bann with the National Weather Service Weather Prediction Center tells Lonsdorf &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6054761:x" target="_blank"&gt;the East Coast storm is the primary concern&lt;/a&gt;. Bann says the storm will become better organized throughout the day, bringing strong winds and heavy rain that could lead to coastal flooding. The good news: Forecasters expect the East Coast's major storm to move on, mostly wrapping up by Saturday, Lonsdorf says.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Trump administration has proposed new tariffs targeting goods from 14 major U.S. trading partners&lt;/strong&gt;, including China, Japan and the European Union. Administration officials argue the measures counter unfair foreign trade practices, though critics question their ultimate effectiveness. Proposed rates may reach 40% on Chinese imports, 35% on Vietnamese goods, and 20-25% on products from other targeted nations. Additional tariffs on Brazilian sugar and aircraft are also being suggested.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;U.S. Trade Ambassador Jamieson Greer said that new tariffs could take effect within a couple of months.&lt;/strong&gt; For each country, the White House has listed a "proposed" rate and a "deal" rate, NPR's Danielle Kurtzleben says. For example, if talks with China progress positively, they may receive a deal rate of 20%, which is different from its proposed rate of 40%. Although the Supreme Court overturned President Trump's previous tariffs, the new ones &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6054761:x" target="_blank"&gt;fall under Section 301&lt;/a&gt;, a law meant to counter unfair trade practices. The administration says these countries exhibit "structural excess capacity" in various manufactured goods, a situation caused by policies that lead to overproduction, which can distort the global market.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Federal scientists are testing the air, soil and water in Eastern Iowa for lead contamination &lt;/strong&gt;after the U.S. Army detonated thousands of pounds of unstable lead azide at the Iowa Army Ammunition Plant in Middletown yesterday. Officials said the controlled explosion was the only safe way to dispose of the bomb-making compound.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;Eliza Billingham of NPR network station Iowa Public Radio says the major concern is the potential release of lead into the air from the explosion.&lt;/strong&gt; She adds that the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency has tested the area since the detonation and hasn't found lead in the air. The EPA has deployed around 300 people to sample the air, ground and nearby water. Lead is a neurotoxin that &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6054761:x" target="_blank"&gt;especially endangers children and pregnant people&lt;/a&gt; because it can impede childhood development. After a week and a half of delays and inconsistent communication from the Army, residents have grown hesitant about the Army and the EPA's initial findings, Billingham says. Residents want independent monitoring and the University of Iowa and the University of Illinois are conducting regional sampling. Results are expected in a few days and should show if their measurements align with the EPA's data, Billingham says.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A federal judge has blocked Trump from challenging the ABC television network's broadcast licenses.&lt;/strong&gt; U.S. District Court Judge Loren AliKhan ruled that the president retaliating against satire and commentary he dislikes is unconstitutional. AliKhan issued the preliminary injunction yesterday and dismissed the administration's request to throw out ABC and Disney's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/26/nx-s1-6000576/fcc-disney-abc-first-amendment-trump-brendan-carr" target="_blank"&gt;lawsuit challenging the review of the local license&lt;/a&gt;. Licenses typically last eight years and are rarely revoked. AliKhan's decision drew heavily on Trump's public statements and social media posts against ABC and Disney, as well as comments from Brendan Carr, the president's pick for chair of the Federal Communications Commission.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Life advice&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-155285" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5333;         --source-height: 3000;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/600/qual