om/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5333x3000+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F58%2Fd6%2Fbb0752e54021b462287041746e6b%2F261124-lk-saynotonew-hedimg-16x9.jpg" class="img" alt="Our brains are wired to seek out newness, and the retail industry is set up to keep us coming back for more as quickly as possible." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Our brains are wired to seek out newness, and the retail industry is set up to keep us coming back for more as quickly as possible.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          J Studios/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Holiday shopping season is in full swing. Before you spend, consider if you actually need what's in your cart. Sales are exciting because our brains are wired to seek newness. Retailers capitalize on that urge. To escape the cycle of constantly wanting more, shop intentionally and appreciate what you already own, says Eric Athas, author of &lt;em&gt;Saying No to New&lt;/em&gt;. He shares his &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/25/nx-s1-6052361/buying-new-things-feels-wonderful-can-be-trap-break-the-cycle" target="_blank"&gt;insights on breaking this cycle&lt;/a&gt; and finding joy in your current possessions with &lt;em&gt;Life Kit&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🛒 Delete the app or remove your credit card info if you have one-click checkout with a company.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🛒 Add an item to your online shopping cart and leave it for 24 hours. Research shows that delaying a purchase decreases your interest in it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🛒 Make intentional choices. Don't reject all new things. After you understand this, you can learn to say no to the wrong items and yes to the right ones.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🛒 Revisiting old things can provide you with untapped enjoyment in them, research has found. You can apply this by rereading a book or by traveling to a city you have visited before.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;For more guidance on how to reclaim joy without seeking newness, &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6023372:x" target="_blank"&gt;listen to this episode of NPR's&lt;em&gt; Life Kit&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Subscribe to &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/life-kit" target="_blank"&gt;the &lt;em&gt;Life Kit&lt;/em&gt; newsletter&lt;/a&gt; for expert advice on love, money, relationships and more.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Picture show&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-155250" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div    