6b%2Fgettyimages-2306395777.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3771x2121+0+196/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7e%2F7a%2F1a6382db43319335b6d467adbb6b%2Fgettyimages-2306395777.jpg" class="img" alt="Aaron Rodgers, wearing a black cap and his Steelers jersey, stands on the field. He is seen from the shoulders up." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Aaron Rodgers #8 of the Pittsburgh Steelers walks off the field after their 19-16 loss to the Philadelphia Eagles at Lincoln Financial Field on Nov. 22, 2026, in Philadelphia.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Emilee Chinn/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Pittsburgh Steelers have &lt;a href="https://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6054185:x" target="_blank"&gt;cut quarterback Aaron Rodgers&lt;/a&gt; after he claimed in an interview that the team's head coach sleeps in meetings.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Ariston Cafe opened in 1924 along Illinois's Route 66, serving classic American diner fare. The National Register &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/25/nx-s1-5983717/ariston-cafe-route-66-diner-litchfield-illinois" target="_blank"&gt;landmark attracts international travelers&lt;/a&gt; and hosts local milestones, from wedding proposals to 65th anniversaries.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;In this week's Far-Flung Postcards, NPR's Emily Feng brings readers &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/25/nx-s1-6051429/mount-kilimanjaro-africa-tanzania" target="_blank"&gt;views of the peak of Mount Kilimanjaro&lt;/a&gt;. She was able to see it during a camping trip at altitude.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
