      <title>Army to detonate tons of lead azide after delays. And, Abrego Garcia leaves U.S.</title>
      <author>Brittney Melton</author>
      <link>https://www.npr.org/2026/11/25/g-s1-155493/up-first-newsletter-iowa-detonation-kilmar-abrego-garcia-nvidia-jensen-huang</link>
      <comments>https://text.npr.org/2026/11/25/g-s1-155493/up-first-newsletter-iowa-detonation-kilmar-abrego-garcia-nvidia-jensen-huang</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.npr.org/2026/11/25/g-s1-155493/up-first-newsletter-iowa-detonation-kilmar-abrego-garcia-nvidia-jensen-huang</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:18:09 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Army will detonate a huge explosion in Middletown, Iowa, this morning&lt;/strong&gt; to safely dispose of thousands of pounds of lead azide that could spontaneously explode. The explosive has been used since WWI and was moved to the Iowa bunker 17 years ago. The detonation is happening after officials found that the lead azide had crystallized and become unstable. Authorities have evacuated a 5-mile radius, and those within 20 miles are advised to stay indoors to avoid exposure to toxins.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-155495-1" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 8667;         --source-height: 4875;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8667x4875+0+446/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff5%2F14%2Fc41a211243cca4495a4be2641da4%2Fgettyimages-2306544716.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8667x4875+0+446/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff5%2F14%2Fc41a211243cca4495a4be2641da4%2Fgettyimages-2306544716.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/cro