resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F3e%2F55%2F5987a64f424b84b128aba38ba342%2Fnpr-lr-stop-thinking-about-work-harlan-3.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4356x2450+0+227/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F3e%2F55%2F5987a64f424b84b128aba38ba342%2Fnpr-lr-stop-thinking-about-work-harlan-3.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4356x2450+0+227/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F3e%2F55%2F5987a64f424b84b128aba38ba342%2Fnpr-lr-stop-thinking-about-work-harlan-3.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4356x2450+0+227/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F3e%2F55%2F5987a64f424b84b128aba38ba342%2Fnpr-lr-stop-thinking-about-work-harlan-3.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4356x2450+0+227/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F3e%2F55%2F5987a64f424b84b128aba38ba342%2Fnpr-lr-stop-thinking-about-work-harlan-3.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4356x2450+0+227/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F3e%2F55%2F5987a64f424b84b128aba38ba342%2Fnpr-lr-stop-thinking-about-work-harlan-3.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4356x2450+0+227/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F3e%2F55%2F5987a64f424b84b128aba38ba342%2Fnpr-lr-stop-thinking-about-work-harlan-3.jpg" class="img" alt="Still photography of a padlock around a laptop. " loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;If you're spending your free time ruminating about work-related issues, you're essentially still on the clock, according to psychologist and author Guy Winch. Don't let workplace woes invade your home life. Winch shares techniques with &lt;em&gt;Life Kit&lt;/em&gt; to &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/21/nx-s1-6043793/stop-thinking-about-work" target="_blank"&gt;help you reclaim your time&lt;/a&gt;, energy and attention when work consumes too much of your mental bandwidth.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🧠 Instead of reliving the work issue, spend 15 minutes creating a plan to address the situation. Ask yourself, "How can I handle this? What outcome do I want?"&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🧠 Adopt rituals that engage as many senses as possible to help your brain transition between tasks. For example, try changing your clothes to signal the end of the workday. The more you repeat rituals, the easier it is for your brain to shift from work to relaxation.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🧠 Do something that energizes you. Activities like screen time and doomscrolling may seem relaxing, but they aren't effective.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🧠 Ask yourself: "If my job disappeared tomorrow, what remains of me?" You might realize your worth isn't tied to your job title.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;For more guidance on how to switch off your work brain, &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6040492:x" target="_blank"&gt;listen to this episode of NPR's&lt;em&gt; Life Kit&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Subscribe to &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/life-kit" target="_blank"&gt;the &lt;em&gt;Life Kit &lt;/em&gt;newsletter&lt;/a&gt; for expert advice on love, money, relationships and more.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-155494" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3696;         --source-height: 2079;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3696x2079+0+193/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F85%2Ffb%2Fccbc8ce944c4bd68f55cd6ffa272%2Fgettyimages-2238199404.jpg" class="img" alt="Ezra Frech of Team United States competes during the Men&amp;#039;s Long Jump T63 Final on three of the World Para Athletics Championships New Delhi 2025 at Jawaharlal Nehru Stadium on Sept. 29, 2025 in New Delhi, India." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Ezra Frech of Team United States competes during the Men's Long Jump T63 Final on  three of the World Para Athletics Championships New Delhi 2025 at Jawaharlal Nehru Stadium on Sept. 29, 2025 in New Delhi, India.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Kenta Harada/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Dancing with the Stars&lt;/em&gt; wrapped up Season 35 last night, crowning Paralympian Ezra Frech and his partner, Daniella Karagach, as the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/25/nx-s1-6052435/dancing-with-the-stars-crowns-new-winner-in-finale" target="_blank"&gt;winners of this year's Len Goodman Mirrorball Trophy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Frailejon, a plant of Colombia's high-mountain wetlands that's vital to the country's water supply, is facing an array of threats from farmers, ranchers and climate change. Volunteers are &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/24/nx-s1-6038806/colombia-water-plants-frailejons" target="_blank"&gt;working to save these plants&lt;/a&gt;, one seedling at a time.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Doctors are &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/24/nx-s1-6001723/vitamin-k-deficiency-refusal-vaccine-misinformation-newborn-bleeding" target="_blank"&gt;combating disinformation about routine vitamin K shots&lt;/a&gt; for newborns, which prevent rare but life-threatening hemorrhaging. The rate of parents skipping these shots for their kids has increased from 3.1% in 2017 to 6.8% in 2025, according to new research in JAMA.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
