pot%2F67%2Fa1%2F2a7c9b0b4b1783ffed73a002a6ad%2Fgettyimages-2283306424.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5265x2962+0+281/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F67%2Fa1%2F2a7c9b0b4b1783ffed73a002a6ad%2Fgettyimages-2283306424.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5265x2962+0+281/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F67%2Fa1%2F2a7c9b0b4b1783ffed73a002a6ad%2Fgettyimages-2283306424.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5265x2962+0+281/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F67%2Fa1%2F2a7c9b0b4b1783ffed73a002a6ad%2Fgettyimages-2283306424.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5265x2962+0+281/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F67%2Fa1%2F2a7c9b0b4b1783ffed73a002a6ad%2Fgettyimages-2283306424.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5265x2962+0+281/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F67%2Fa1%2F2a7c9b0b4b1783ffed73a002a6ad%2Fgettyimages-2283306424.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5265x2962+0+281/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F67%2Fa1%2F2a7c9b0b4b1783ffed73a002a6ad%2Fgettyimages-2283306424.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5265x2962+0+281/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F67%2Fa1%2F2a7c9b0b4b1783ffed73a002a6ad%2Fgettyimages-2283306424.jpg" class="img" alt="Bottles of Roundup weed killer are displayed on a shelf at a Home Depot store on June 25, 2026 in North Hollywood, California." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Bottles of Roundup weed killer are displayed on a shelf at a Home Depot store on June 25, 2026 in North Hollywood, California.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Justin Sullivan/Getty Images North America                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Bayer could &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/21/nx-s1-6049684/roundup-bayer-hodgkins-settlement" target="_blank"&gt;pay up to $7.25 billion&lt;/a&gt; to settle lawsuits alleging that its weed-killer Roundup caused cancer. A Missouri judge gave final approval to the nationwide settlement.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;South Africa's grassroots program Read Alex is &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/22/g-s1-154387/books-children-authors-south-africa-literacy" target="_blank"&gt;tackling a children's literacy crisis&lt;/a&gt; and inspiring kids to write. The initiative culminated in a book launch for an anthology titled&lt;em&gt; From Gomora to the World&lt;/em&gt;, showcasing stories written by children.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Orchestra Noir &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/20/g-s1-154644/orchestra-noir-black-musical-tour-classical-music" target="_blank"&gt;transforms 2000s hip-hop and R&amp;B classics&lt;/a&gt; into high-energy, choreographed symphonic shows. Beyond delivering performances, the all-Black ensemble creates a cultural bridge through their post-show ritual, when musicians meet with their multigenerational audiences.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
