strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2Ff6%2F57%2F1cdfc9bb4447a18aa5df06a032bf%2Fgettyimages-2305571337.jpg" class="img" alt="Hakeem Jeffries, D-N.Y., speaks during a news conference in the U.S. Capitol on Nov. 17, 2026 in Washington, DC. Jeffries spoke on a range of topics including the upcoming leadership elections for the House Democrats. (Photo by Anna Moneymaker/Getty Images)" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Hakeem Jeffries, D-N.Y., speaks during a news conference in the U.S. Capitol on Nov. 17, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Anna Moneymaker/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧&lt;strong&gt; Jeffries, who has served as the top Democrat&lt;/strong&gt; in the minority since 2023, ran unopposed for the speaker position. But that is &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6047056:x" target="_blank"&gt;not the case in the Senate&lt;/a&gt;, NPR's Elena Moore tells&lt;em&gt; Up First&lt;/em&gt;. Current minority leader Sen. Chuck Schumer faces a challenge from Sen. Chris Van Hollen for majority leader. Van Hollen has positioned himself as an anti-status quo, progressive leader. Both Van Hollen and Schumer have served in Congress for decades. The vote for that Senate position is set for early December.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;➡️ &lt;strong&gt;Rep. Robert Garcia, poised to chair the House Oversight Committee, sent document-preservation letters&lt;/strong&gt; to more than a dozen of President Trump's allies and family members in preparation for investigations starting in January. These &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/18/g-s1-154147/robert-garcia-house-democrats-investigations-trump-administration" target="_blank"&gt;letters focus on four main areas&lt;/a&gt;: "Trump family corruption, corporate corruption, DHS misconduct and the White House Epstein cover-up."&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trump, Russian President Vladimir Putin and Chinese President Xi Jinping met today&lt;/strong&gt; in Shenzhen, China, on the sidelines of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation forum. Xi and Putin met separately the night before &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/18/nx-s1-6040432/trump-xi-and-putin-shenzhen-china-russia-usa" target="_blank"&gt;the trilateral meeting&lt;/a&gt;. Trump also had one-on-one meetings with Putin and Xi. It's the first time the three leaders have held a summit together.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;The three leaders had different agendas as they went into their meeting&lt;/strong&gt;, NPR's Jennifer Pak says. Trump aimed to &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6047056:x" target="_blank"&gt;prioritize nuclear arms control&lt;/a&gt;. He said that they had a unique opportunity to reduce nuclear weapons, a stance Beijing has typically resisted due to its smaller stockpile compared to the U.S. and Russia. Putin sought discussions to end the war in Ukraine, but on Moscow's terms. The complexity of these issues makes substantial outcomes unlikely, Pak says. Xi aimed to position China as a stabilizing global force by bringing together Russia, its old ally, and the U.S., its direct competitor.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anthropic is set to debut on the Nasdaq exchange today. &lt;/strong&gt;The company raised more than $100 billion in a &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/19/nx-s1-6042558/anthropic-ipo-breaks-records-100-billion" target="_blank"&gt;record-breaking initial public offering&lt;/a&gt; that valued the company at around $1.5 trillion. The company sold 956 million shares at $83 each, surpassing its initial target range of $70 to $78. The seven founders sold over 23 million shares as part of the IPO, and the company's prospectus outlines plans to introduce an extra $26 billion in shares through private placements with Google, Microsoft and Nvidia.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧&lt;strong&gt; In its IPO filing, Anthropic was optimistic that AI would have a bigger impact &lt;/strong&gt;on the economy than industrialization, electricity, semiconductors and the internet, NPR's John Ruwitch says. The company's paperwork suggested that the addressable market for Anthropic's products &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-6047056:x" target="_blank"&gt;could be as big as $40 trillion annually&lt;/a&gt;, exceeding the GDP of the United States. But CEO Dario Amodei has been outspoken about the danger of losing control over AI. The prospectus flagged some political risks, including the company's current dispute with the Pentagon over how its models can be used. Ruwitch says that now that Anthropic and SpaceX are on the market, OpenAI could potentially join next year.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Watch this&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-154339" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2600;         --source-height: 1463;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1200/qualit