+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2600x1463+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F7c%2Fe4%2F879eb0894f17898f348557f452c2%2Fnewmakers-benshapiro-clean.png" class="img" alt="Ben Shapiro sits with NPR for a Newsmakers interview. He wears a dark gray suit jacket and light brown shirt." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Ben Shapiro sits with NPR for a &lt;em&gt;Newsmakers&lt;/em&gt; interview.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Nickolai Hammar/NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Go face-to-face with the person of the moment. NPR's &lt;/em&gt;Newsmakers&lt;em&gt; video podcast brings the biggest names in politics, business, sports, arts, and culture out of the headlines and into the interview chair to discuss the mark they're making on the world. Follow the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/g-s1-114952/nprs-newsmakers" target="_blank"&gt;Newsmakers&lt;em&gt; podcast&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; or subscribe to &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/npr" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;NPR's YouTube channel&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to get new episodes as soon as they're available.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Ben Shapiro says he remains committed to his values during Trump's turbulent presidency. The conservative podcast host voted against Trump in 2016, but actively campaigned for him in 2024. Shapiro expressed disappointment in the president's tariffs, alleged corruption and the handling of the war in Iran. He says that Trump's strict immigration policies and the "whiff of corruption" surrounding the White House contributed to the GOP's midterm losses. The co-founder of the media company &lt;em&gt;The Daily Wire &lt;/em&gt;warns that Republicans face an "uphill road in 2028," and he doesn't see Vice President JD Vance as the right GOP presidential candidate. Shapiro argues that Vance could alienate key voter groups like Hispanics, the working class, women and the college-educated. In conversation with &lt;em&gt;Morning Edition&lt;/em&gt;'s Steve Inskeep, Shapiro discussed who he thinks could be a potential 2028 GOP candidate, his new movie, &lt;em&gt;Confession,&lt;/em&gt; and the recent decline in his show's YouTube subscriptions.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://lnk.to/mcjn3cNW" target="_blank"&gt;Watch or listen&lt;/a&gt; to the interview or &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/19/nx-s1-6034593/ben-shapiro-gop-midterms-losses-trump" target="_blank"&gt;read the article&lt;/a&gt; about their discussion.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's listen&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-154213" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 7452;         --source-height: 4192;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7452x4192+0+389/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F6c%2Fbe%2F85fb4b2d4132bf92577c8a5fd3c3%2Fgettyimages-2304057968.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7452x4192+0+389/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F6c%2Fbe%2F85fb4b2d4132bf92577c8a5fd3c3%2Fgettyimages-2304057968.jpg 600w, https://n