ttps://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7452x4192+0+389/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F6c%2Fbe%2F85fb4b2d4132bf92577c8a5fd3c3%2Fgettyimages-2304057968.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7452x4192+0+389/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F6c%2Fbe%2F85fb4b2d4132bf92577c8a5fd3c3%2Fgettyimages-2304057968.jpg" class="img" alt="The West-Eastern Divan Orchestra at the Pierre Boulez Hall at the Barenboim-Said Academy. A woman wearing a bright blue shawl stands next to a man wearing a black shirt. A woman sits to their right, wearing a white shirt and holding a violin. More people are sitting in chairs around the room." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Israeli violist Tal Riva Theodorou (C-L) arrives for a rehearsal of the West-Eastern Divan Orchestra at the Pierre Boulez Hall at the Barenboim-Said Academy in Berlin on Nov. 9, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Odd Andersen/AFP via Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The West-Eastern Divan Orchestra is an ensemble founded by Edward Said and Daniel Barenboim nearly 30 years ago in Germany to unite Middle Eastern musicians. Despite the deep personal grief and heightened tensions following the Hamas-led attack on Israel on Oct. 7, 2023, and the Gaza war, members of the orchestra strive to confront, rather than sidestep, political realities. Longtime musicians say Barenboim has helped them bridge painful cultural divides and foster enduring cross-border friendships. The space has also given some participants a safe space to discuss Gaza, &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i//nx-s1-6043148:x" target="_blank"&gt;allowing music to resolve&lt;/a&gt; the dissonance.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-154329" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2000;         --source-height: 1125;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+223/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F4f%2F56%2F780b10f04562af1b3d88378e203d%2Fabdelrahman-elgendy-credit-fadel-dawod-1.png 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+223/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F4f%2F56%2F780b10f04562af1b3d88378e203d%2Fabdelrahman-elgendy-credit-fadel-dawod-1.png 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+223/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F4f%2F56%2F780b10f04562af1b3d88378e203d%2Fabdelrahman-elgendy-credit-fadel-dawod-1.png 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+223/resize/900/quality/85/forma