ldcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg" class="img" alt="Dressed in costumes for Halloween, students of Kids Campus SFCC play at the playground in Santa Fe, New Mexico." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Dressed in costumes for Halloween, students of Kids Campus SFCC play at the playground in Santa Fe, New Mexico.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Nina Alexandria Riggio for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;One year ago, New Mexico became the first state to offer free childcare to all families regardless of income, as long as adults are working, seeking work, in school, or unable to work. Many parents have found this initiative life-changing, but capacity was limited. Only 50% of the some 67,000 children ages 5 and under are enrolled in the universal childcare program. Some of the remaining families participate in other programs, such as PreK and Head Start. New Mexico officials say the program must expand to meet demand. The issues observed in New Mexico are mirrored across the nation, prompting policymakers and childcare advocates to &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/15/nx-s1-6040194/new-mexico-free-universal-childcare-families" target="_blank"&gt;closely monitor the state's initiative&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;👶 Almost half of U.S. children aged 5 and under live in licensed childcare deserts, where demand exceeds availability, according to the Center for American Progress, a left-leaning think tank.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;👶 New Mexico's program has an operating budget of nearly $600 million, but some lawmakers are concerned it could be $50 million over budget this year.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;👶 New Mexico state Sen. Steve Lanier tells NPR that the steep cost of the program is why he only supports universal childcare for some people, since someone earning around $450,000 or $600,000 might not need assistance. Lanier has previously sued to end the initiative, but the lawsuit was unsuccessful.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;👶 Since the enactment of free, universal childcare in New Mexico, lower-income mothers have experienced significant gains. Their full-time employment has risen by 23%, according to a new paper from Arizona State University.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;       &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Picture show&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-153583-1" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 7440;         --source-height: 4185;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7440x4185+0+389/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2Fe0%2F3d5979dc4a7ca8677703331dfaec%2Funiversalchildcare-npr-10-30-2026-177.jpg" class="img" alt="Dressed in costumes for Halloween, students of Kids Campus SFCC play at the playground in Santa Fe, New Mexico." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Dressed in costumes for Halloween, students of Kids Campus SFCC play at the playground in Santa Fe, New Mexico.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Nina Alexandria Riggio for NPR                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Millions of shorebirds embark on epic migrations to Alaska each year to breed. They often travel thousands of miles from places like New Zealand, Asia and South America. But researchers have found a concerning trend: Nearly half of the 41 shorebird species that breed in Alaska are in decline. These birds time their journeys to coincide with peak insect availability, and climate change is throwing off their schedules. Warmer springs lead to earlier insect emergence, creating a mismatch that could leave shorebirds without enough food supply. Scientists are now racing to understand if these migratory birds can &lt;a href="http://www.npr.org/2026/11/16/nx-s1-6020923/arctic-bird-migration-alaska-climate-change" target="_blank"&gt;adapt to the changing Arctic landscape&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-153856" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 7589;         --source-height: 4266;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/1100/quality/50/format/webp/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/7589x4266+0+137/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fnpr-production-npr.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com%2Fbrightspot%2F18%2Fa4%2Fcc4619ed445f9322e6fe0efcc7b9%2Fgettyimages-2284931307.jpg" class="img" alt="Robert Pattinson attends the world premiere of The Odyssey in London in July." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Robert Pattinson attends the world premiere of &lt;em&gt;The Odyssey&lt;/em&gt; in London in July.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Gareth Cattermole/Getty Images Europe                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;British actor Robert Pattinson will be the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/16/nx-s1-6042420/james-bond-casting-robert-pattinson" target="_blank"&gt;seventh James Bond&lt;/a&gt;, taking his place among an iconic lineup of stars that started with Sean Connery and most recently featured Daniel Craig.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The 69th annual Grammy Awards nominations were announced yesterday. British singer-songwriter RAYE &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/11/16/nx-s1-6037518/2027-grammy-nominations-complete-list" target="_blank"&gt;leads with 11 nominations&lt;/a&gt;, followed by Spanish artist Rosalía with nine nods.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Civil rights champion Dolores Huerta made history yesterday as the first non-elected individual and the &lt;a href="https://www.kqed.org/news/12109686/dolores-huerta-to-make-history-as-first-woman-to-lie-in-honor-at-california-state-capitol" target="_blank"&gt;first woman to lie in honor&lt;/a&gt; at the California State Capitol. She died of cancer last month at age 96. (via &lt;a href="https://www.kqed.org/" target="_blank"&gt;KQED&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
